    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d262">

                <pb facs="0330" n="214" sameAs="frus:frus1914/pg214"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 839.00/1078.</note>
                <head ana="#head_untitled-inferred-from-preceding-sibling-head">[Untitled]</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Legation</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Santo Domingo</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-03-04T14:00:00-04:40">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">March 4, 1914, 2 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Have persuaded President Bordas to make last appeal to Arias. <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Petrel</hi> sails tonight with Bordas and Lovaton. I
                    believe surpassing effrontery and egotism of Arias makes agreement out of the
                    question. Bordas will not permit Horacio Vasquez to return under tense
                    circumstances fearing further revolutionary activities on his part. Claimed
                    country must be handled firmly else anarchy will follow. Provisional Government
                    can subdue sanguinary element if you give it means.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sullivan</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
